-**Definitions:**
-*   **View Vector:** $\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{p}) = \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{p}$.
-*   **Orientation Function:** $\psi_{\phi, \mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{p}) := \langle \nabla \phi(\mathbf{p}), \mathbf{v}(\mathbf{p}) \rangle$. This function is zero where the surface normal is perpendicular to the view direction [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Primary Edge Set:** $S := \{ \mathbf{p} \mid \phi(\mathbf{p}) = 0, \psi_{\phi, \mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{p}) = 0 \}$. This is the intersection of the surface and the orientation function [S1][S2, unofficial].
+*   **AABB:** Defined by minimum and maximum coordinates. Used for range analysis to bound the search space [S1].
+*   **Orientation Function $\psi$:** Defined as $\psi_{\phi, \mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{p}) := \langle \nabla \phi(\mathbf{p}), \mathbf{v}_{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{p}) \rangle$, where $\mathbf{v}_{\mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{p}) = \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{p}$ is the view vector [S1]. The primary boundary $S$ is the set $\{ \mathbf{p} \mid \phi(\mathbf{p}) = 0, \psi_{\phi, \mathbf{c}}(\mathbf{p}) = 0 \}$ [S1].
 
 **Parameters:**
